# IsItStable — Set Version Verdict

When the Emperor (or anyone) says "give vX.Y.Z a stable/unstable verdict", follow this — do **not** create a new issue.

## Background

OPERATOR_POD runs daily and pre-creates one issue per detected version:

```
[vX.Y.Z] [pkg] Is it stable?
labels: version, pkg:<name>, verdict:pending
```

Issuing a verdict = relabel `verdict:pending` → `verdict:yes` or `verdict:no`.
The site is **SSG + `data/versions.json`** (not live GitHub queries) — you must trigger `sync.yml` after the relabel, which then curls the Vercel deploy hook.

## Steps

### 1. Find the existing issue

```bash
gh issue list --repo exisz/IsItStable --search "<version>" \
  --json number,title,labels --state all
```

Match the title `[v<version>] [<pkg>] Is it stable?`. If multiple packages,
disambiguate by `pkg:` label.

**If no issue exists:** the version was missed by OPERATOR_POD. Check
`projects/isitstable-com/` for the operator schedule before creating one
manually — likely a pod bug to fix instead.

### 2. Swap the verdict label

```bash
gh issue edit <N> --repo exisz/IsItStable \
  --remove-label "verdict:pending" \
  --add-label "verdict:yes"   # or verdict:no
```

### 3. Trigger sync

```bash
gh workflow run sync.yml --repo exisz/IsItStable
```

`sync.yml` rebuilds `data/versions.json` and pings the Vercel deploy hook.
Without this step, the website does not update.

### 4. (Optional) Add a verdict comment

For non-trivial verdicts, drop a short comment on the issue explaining why
(known bug references, regression notes, etc.). This shows up on the
version detail page.

## Anti-Patterns

- ❌ Creating a new issue with `gh issue create --label verdict:yes`. The
  OPERATOR_POD-created issue is the canonical one and already has reactions /
  bug references attached. A new issue duplicates and orphans existing votes.
- ❌ Editing the label without triggering `sync.yml` — site stays stale.
- ❌ Using the GitHub UI's Projects-style "single-select option mutation" —
  see MEMORY.md lesson on how that wipes all field values.

## Quick One-Liner

```bash
V=2026.5.3-1 VERDICT=yes && \
N=$(gh issue list --repo exisz/IsItStable --search "$V" --state all --json number -q '.[0].number') && \
gh issue edit "$N" --repo exisz/IsItStable --remove-label verdict:pending --add-label "verdict:$VERDICT" && \
gh workflow run sync.yml --repo exisz/IsItStable
```
